  "scope": "Synthetic source includes 5000 ledger-tracked deterministic files of 4096 bytes each. Production collector with retained auxiliary monitoring, native preparation, canonical coverage and acknowledgement. Optional export includes encryption and built-in exact-ciphertext verification; import includes its trust-boundary verification. Excludes fixture setup/mutation, network transfer/remote proof and energy. File population and byte sizes are explicit fixture parameters; synthetic file bytes do not establish real-media type/content diversity. Storage counters are Darwin process-attributed I/O; cached reads can be zero and buffered attribution can cross stage boundaries. Optional SQLite counters cover only canonical producer/importer Cache connections, not native mirrors or source readers; cache_writes/spills are page counts and cache_bytes is a gauge. Disabling spills is an explicit benchmark-only experiment. RSS is the lifetime peak including fixture/baseline, not incremental-only peak. Ciphertext bytes are potential transfer bytes, not measured network traffic.",
